Step 1: Download and Extract
PowerShell
Invoke-WebRequest -Uri 'https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy/releases/download/v2.4/scrcpy-win64-v2.4.zip' -OutFile "$HOME\OneDrive\Desktop\scrcpy.zip"
Expand-Archive -Path "$HOME\OneDrive\Desktop\scrcpy.zip" -DestinationPath "$HOME\OneDrive\Desktop\scrcpy" -Force

Step 2: Navigate to the Folder
PowerShell
Set-Location "$HOME\OneDrive\Desktop\scrcpy\scrcpy-win64-v2.4"

Step 3: Check Your Phone Connection
PowerShell
.\adb.exe devices
If your phone shows a prompt asking "Allow USB debugging?", tap Allow (and check "Always allow").

Step 4: Launch Screen Mirroring & Control
PowerShell
.\scrcpy.exe
A live window of your phone screen will open on your laptop, allowing full mouse clicks, swipes, and laptop keyboard typing. In the future, you can also just open that scrcpy folder on your desktop and double-click scrcpy.exe.


Your full phone screen will instantly display in a smooth, high-resolution window on your laptop desktop. You can click to open apps, swipe with your mouse, type on your physical laptop keyboard, and control the entire device in real time.
